  "description": "The 2026 election for New York's 15th Congressional District, based in the South Bronx, features a competitive Democratic primary between incumbent Rep. Ritchie Torres (D) and challengers Michael Blake and Jose Vega, with the primary scheduled for June 23, 2026. Torres, first elected in 2020, has drawn criticism from the left over his staunch support for Israel and centrist pivots, while Blake and Vega are running on platforms emphasizing affordability, cost of living, and a more progressive foreign policy. The Republican nominee is Stylo A. Sapaskis, who advanced without a primary, and independent Andre Easton is also on the general election ballot. The district is heavily Democratic (Cook PVI: D+27), so the Democratic primary is effectively the decisive contest, though the general election will be held on November 3, 2026.",
